From 0220e92afdf7bac39dc2a76c10106dbc7cc287b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ttabouch12 <ttabouch12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:17:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] power: supply: sm5705_charger: add Silicon Mitus SM5705
 charger driver

Add a power_supply driver for the charger cell of the SM5705 MFD. It
reports online, status, charge type, health and the programmed limits,
and handles the VBUS, battery and thermal interrupts of the chip.

The float voltage and termination current come from monitored-battery.
The input current limit and the fast charge current are selected from
conservative devicetree limits (vendor defaults) according to the cable
reported by the MUIC extcon device, falling back to the SDP limits. The
chip's top-off timer, auto-stop, AICL and thermal protection are enabled
as in the vendor driver; the charge safety timers are left untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C7LhHWjrzX28CzyNMEnVDk
